# ── DEVELOPMENT (local only) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loaded by: npm run dev
#
# Leave the two Supabase values EMPTY. With no credentials the repository
# resolves to localStore (src/data/store/repository.js) and the console runs on
# browser localStorage with demo data. That is the intended local setup:
#
#   • free — it uses none of your Supabase project allowance
#   • safe — it cannot read a real customer or write a real invoice, and cannot
#     advance the live GST document counter
#   • complete — every module works; click "Load demo data" on the dashboard
#
# Sign in with any email and the passphrase `ortex@admin` (the offline gate,
# not Supabase auth). The login screen states this when no database is set.
#
# Only fill these in if you deliberately want local work against a real
# database, and then never point them at production.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Badge, so this is never mistaken for the live console.
VITE_ENV_LABEL=Local demo
